Research Computing facilities & support are an [[color:red][essential]] and [[color:cyan][integral]] component of a research university.

#+ATTR_REVEAL: :frag (appear)
For this reason, and to support student development skills and basic/PoC usage, e-Research facilities and support have [[color:yellow][free-to-use]] components:

#+ATTR_REVEAL: :frag (appear)
- [[color:lime][HPC]]: free to use, resources shared with queue scheduler
- [[color:lightsalmon][RDS]]: free 5 TB per funded project
- [[color:orange][Private cloud/IaaS]]: small vCPU and memory projects

** Costing model

Costing model based upon TRAC methodology; some components are TRAC-listed, and others aren't

#+ATTR_REVEAL: :frag (appear)
- [[color:magenta][pay-as-you-go GPU]] usage model (£0.12-£0.98 per hour)
- [[color:navajowhite][GPU/CPU server]] hosting (£2,194-£3,275 per server)
- [[color:tan][RDS]] (£16.36-£60 per TB per year)
- [[color:gold][Private Cloud]]

More information at: https://docs.er.kcl.ac.uk/costing_grants/

